{
  "id": 491605754,
  "iid": 25215,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "TLS: Fix calculation of client traffic secret in psk_ke",
  "description": "The client traffic secret is derived using the handshake hash\nas it exists at the Server Finished, and does not include\nEndOfEarlyData or the Client Certificate, CertificateVerify,\nor Finished handshake messages. The only secret derived using\nthe entire handshake transcript to the Client Finished is the\nresumption master secret, but we don't support resuming with\nPSKs (yet), so stop collecting the transcript after the Server\nFinished.\n\nhttps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8446#section-4.4.1\nhttps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8446#section-7.1\n\nFixup 4dcf948bdb06e7fa9c91fb4727a790f15d122972\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
